API-10: shift tank rule premises once in reindextanks

reindextanks() moves every tank and reservoir down by ndiff slots when
fewer junctions were created than the file listed. It called
adjusttankrules(pr, -ndiff) inside the loop over tanks, but that
function shifts every tank premise at once, so each premise moved by
ndiff times the number of tanks. The call now follows the loop.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-10_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/validate.c b/src/validate.c
index fb99249..517be03 100644
--- a/src/validate.c
+++ b/src/validate.c
@@ -393,9 +393,11 @@ void reindextanks(Project *pr)
                 control = &net->Control[j];
                 if (control->Node == n1) control->Node = n2;
             }
-            adjusttankrules(pr, -ndiff);
             if (qual->TraceNode == n1) qual->TraceNode = n2;
         }
+
+        // Shift tank indexes in rule premises (all tanks at once)
+        adjusttankrules(pr, -ndiff);
         
         // Reallocate the Node array (shouldn't fail as new size < old size)
         parser->MaxJuncs = net->Njuncs;
